          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What makes an incline trainer different from a regular treadmill?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
              A regular treadmill typically inclines up to 10-15%, mostly to
              add resistance to a walk or jog. An incline trainer like the
              X22i goes dramatically further, from -6% decline to 40%
              incline, which is steep enough to simulate real hiking trails
              and mountain terrain rather than just a slight ramp. That range
              fundamentally changes the kind of training you can do at home,
              from steep hill-walking sessions to downhill running mechanics
              you can't replicate on a flat deck.
            </p>
